Q: Using prepopulated form, submit only changed fields A: <p>Yet another approach, which is a lighter weight version of the accepted answer by @<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/users/2383529/waldol1">waldol1</a> , is to simply omit the &quot;name&quot; attribute from the HTML fields. An &quot;onChange&quot; event listener simply creates the &quot;name&quot; attribute, copied from the &quot;id&quot; attribute, when a change is detected. It works because an HTML field with no &quot;name&quot; attribute is not sent back to the server. Something like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;myField1&quot; value=&quot;value1&quot; onchange=&quot;changeListener( this.id )&quot; &gt;
&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;myField2&quot; value=&quot;value2&quot; onchange=&quot;changeListener( this.id )&quot; &gt;
</code></pre>
<pre><code>function changeListener(fieldId) {
  const field = document.getElementById(fieldId);
  if ( field) {
    const id = field.getAttribute(&quot;id&quot;);
    if( id ) field.setAttribute(&quot;name&quot;, id ) ;
    console.log(`added attribute &quot;name&quot; to ${fieldId}`);
  }
}
</code></pre>
